  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Which of the following is the negation of the statement: For all \\(x\\) of a certain set, \\(x^2\\gt0?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "For all \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\lt0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "For all \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\leq0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "For no \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\gt0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "For some \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\gt0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "For some \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\leq0\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The negation of a universal statement is an existential statement, and the negation of \\(x^2\\gt0\\) is \\(x^2\\leq0.\\) Thus the negation is: for some \\(x,\\) \\(x^2\\leq0.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "The negation of “for all” begins with “for some”",
        "Negating \\(x^2\\gt0\\) gives \\(x^2\\leq0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
